{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 947 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9fabf539487e4949ffa8897ff4a28abf8c43e381f9c05aedb90e5db4f384989e" :edb/db-before-t 946 :edb/db-after-t 947 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534259 50 #inst "2026-10-11T18:21:08.516Z" 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186124539 1038 #edb/ref 17592186416399 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186124541 1038 #edb/ref 17592186416396 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186124541 1038 #edb/ref 17592186416397 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186124576 1038 #edb/ref 17592186416398 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186125123 1068 #edb/ref 17592186123338 13194139534259 17592186045417 false] [17592186125123 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416391 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186125123 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186125123 1071 "Let $B$ be a basis of $R^{2}$ and let $T: R^{2} → R^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T]_{B}$, given that\n\n$T(\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}) = \\begin{bmatrix}x + 3y \\\\ 2x - y\\end{bmatrix}$ and $B = {\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}$." 13194139534259 17592186045417 false] [17592186125123 1071 "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}x+3y \\\\ 2x-y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.$" 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186125123 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -14 & -14\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{7}{4} & -\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{7}{4} & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{7}{4} & -\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4} & -\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{4} & -\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416400 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416401 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416402 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416403 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1043 #edb/ref 17592186416404 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1045 "The Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis" 13194139534259 17592186045417 true] [17592186416365 1046 #edb/ref 17592186416402 13194139534259 175921860454